Patch for @neo4j/graphql 7.2.0 (Apache License 2.0; Copyright (c) "Neo4j", Neo4j Sweden AB).
Modified by Dethernety.

Change: CompositeReadOperation starts each UNION branch of an interface or union relationship
selection with `WITH <parent node>` instead of `WITH *`, as CompositeConnectionReadOperation and
CompositeAggregationOperation in the same package already do. One token in one file; the changed
line carries a notice.

Reason: on Memgraph, `WITH *` at the start of a UNION branch inside a CALL subquery does not carry
the outer variable into the branch, so each branch matches every target of the edge type in the
database instead of the parent node's own. Selecting a relationship field typed by an interface
(here Exposure.element, Analysis.element, Control.elements, Data.elements, Model.representedBy)
then returns unrelated elements. Neo4j is not affected; the patched form returns the same result
on both engines.

Upstream report: to Memgraph, not yet filed.

The patch is keyed to version 7.2.0 exactly and is not applied to any other version. Moving
@neo4j/graphql off 7.2.0 means re-checking this patch against the new version; dt-ws's
src/gql/__tests__/interface-selection-cypher.spec.ts fails on any install without the fix.

diff --git a/dist/translate/queryAST/ast/operations/composite/CompositeReadOperation.js b/dist/translate/queryAST/ast/operations/composite/CompositeReadOperation.js
--- a/dist/translate/queryAST/ast/operations/composite/CompositeReadOperation.js
+++ b/dist/translate/queryAST/ast/operations/composite/CompositeReadOperation.js
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
             const result = c.transpile(context);
             let clauses = result.clauses;
             if (parentNode) {
-                clauses = clauses.map((sq) => cypher_builder_1.default.utils.concat(new cypher_builder_1.default.With("*"), sq));
+                clauses = clauses.map((sq) => cypher_builder_1.default.utils.concat(new cypher_builder_1.default.With(parentNode), sq)); // Modified by Dethernety: start each union branch from the parent node, as the sibling operations do (Memgraph drops the outer scope under WITH *)
             }
             return clauses;
         });
